    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $f(x) = 3x^2-2$ and $g(f(x)) = x^2 + x +1$. Find the sum of all possible values of $g(25)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 13\nB. 25\nC. 15\nD. 9\nE. 18\nF. 19\nG. 22\nH. 21\nI. 20\nJ. 17\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given $ f(x) = 3x^2 - 2 $ and $ g(f(x)) = x^2 + x + 1 $. We want to find $ g(25) $, so we first solve $ f(x) = 25 $:\n$$\n3x^2 - 2 = 25 \\Rightarrow 3x^2 = 27 \\Rightarrow x^2 = 9 \\Rightarrow x = \\pm 3.\n$$\nNow evaluate $ g(f(x)) = x^2 + x + 1 $ at $ x = 3 $ and $ x = -3 $:\n- If $ x = 3 $: $ g(f(3)) = 3^2 + 3 + 1 = 13 $,\n- If $ x = -3 $: $ g(f(-3)) = (-3)^2 + (-3) + 1 = 9 - 3 + 1 = 7 $.\n\nSo $ g(25) $ could be 13 or 7, and the sum of all possible values is $ 13 + 7 = 20 $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
