  {
    "global index": "MathQA_436",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 12 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 10\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the cut be made at a point $ x $ meters from one end, where $ 0 < x < 12 $. The two pieces are $ x $ and $ 12 - x $; assume without loss of generality that the longer piece is used, so we take $ \\max(x, 12 - x) $. This longer piece forms the perimeter of a square, so its side is $ \\frac{\\text{longer piece}}{4} $, and the area is $ \\left(\\frac{\\text{longer piece}}{4}\\right)^2 $. We want the area $ > 4 $, so:\n\n$$\n\\left(\\frac{L}{4}\\right)^2 > 4 \\Rightarrow \\frac{L^2}{16} > 4 \\Rightarrow L^2 > 64 \\Rightarrow L > 8\n$$\n\nSo the longer piece must be greater than 8 meters. Since the total length is 12, the longer piece exceeds 8 when the cut is made such that either $ x > 8 $ or $ 12 - x > 8 $ (i.e., $ x < 4 $). So the favorable region is $ x \\in (0, 4) \\cup (8, 12) $, which has total length $ 4 + 4 = 8 $. The total possible cut points are over 12 meters, so the probability is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 162,
        "output_tokens": 331,
        "total_tokens": 493
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 4.4602000000000004e-05,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": true
  },
  {
    "global index": "MathQA_436",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 12 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 10\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "z-ai/glm-4.7",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the probability that the area of the square is more than 4, we first determine the required length of the wire piece used for the square. Let the side of the square be $s$. The area is $s^2$, and we want $s^2 > 4$, which implies $s > 2$. The perimeter of the square is $4s$, which corresponds to the length of the longer piece of the wire. Therefore, the longer piece must be longer than $4 \\times 2 = 8$ meters.\n\nLet $x$ be the length of one of the pieces created by the cut. The longer piece is $\\max(x, 12 - x)$. We need $\\max(x, 12 - x) > 8$.\nThis inequality holds true in two cases:\n1.  $x > 8$ (meaning the first piece is the longer one).\n2.  $12 - x > 8$, which simplifies to $x < 4$ (meaning the second piece is the longer one).\n\nAssuming the cut is made uniformly at random along the 12-meter wire, the total sample space is the interval $[0, 12]$. The favorable outcomes are the intervals $[0, 4)$ and $(8, 12]$. The length of the favorable interval is $(4 - 0) + (12 - 8) = 8$ meters.\n\nThe probability is the ratio of the favorable length to the total length:\n$$P = \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{2}{3}$$\n\nThis matches option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 157,
        "output_tokens": 2341,
        "total_tokens": 2498
