    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given a linear homogeneous recurrence relation:  \n$ y[n] - 3y[n-1] + 2y[n-2] = 0 $ for $ n \\geq 2 $, with initial conditions $ y[0] = 2 $, $ y[1] = 3 $.  \nUsing the recurrence:  \n$ y[2] = 3y[1] - 2y[0] = 3(3) - 2(2) = 9 - 4 = 5 $,  \n$ y[3] = 3y[2] - 2y[1] = 3(5) - 2(3) = 15 - 6 = 9 $,  \n$ y[4] = 3y[3] - 2y[2] = 3(9) - 2(5) = 27 - 10 = 17 $.  \nSo the sequence for $ n \\geq 2 $ is $ 5, 9, 17, \\dots $, matching option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
