    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10428",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Fouriertransformmethods to find the time-domain responseof a network having a system function [(j2\\omega) / (1 + 2j\\omega)], ifthe input is V(t) =cost (For asinusodialinputcost, the Fourier transform is \\pi[\\delta (\\omega + 1) + \\delta (\\omega - 1)] ).\n\nOptions: \nA. (4/5)cost - (2/5) sin t\nB. (3/4)cost - (1/4)sint\nC. (2/5)cost + (4/5) sin t\nD. cost + sint\nE. (3/5)cost + (1/5)sint\nF. (4/5)cost + (2/5) sin t\nG. (1/5)cost - (3/5)sint\nH. (1/2)cost + (1/2)sint\nI. (1/3)cost - (2/3)sint\nJ. (2/5)cost - (4/5) sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We use the Fourier transform of the input $ V(t) = \\cos t $, which is $ \\pi[\\delta(\\omega + 1) + \\delta(\\omega - 1)] $. The system function is $ H(j\\omega) = \\frac{j2\\omega}{1 + 2j\\omega} $. The output in the frequency domain is $ Y(j\\omega) = H(j\\omega) \\cdot \\mathcal{F}\\{\\cos t\\} $, so we evaluate $ H(j\\omega) $ at $ \\omega = \\pm 1 $:\n\nAt $ \\omega = 1 $:  \n$ H(j1) = \\frac{j2(1)}{1 + 2j(1)} = \\frac{2j}{1 + 2j} \\cdot \\frac{1 - 2j}{1 - 2j} = \\frac{2j(1 - 2j)}{1 + 4} = \\frac{2j - 4j^2}{5} = \\frac{2j + 4}{5} = \\frac{4}{5} + j\\frac{2}{5} $\n\nAt $ \\omega = -1 $:  \n$ H(-j1) = \\frac{j2(-1)}{1 + 2j(-1)} = \\frac{-2j}{1 - 2j} \\cdot \\frac{1 + 2j}{1 + 2j} = \\frac{-2j(1 + 2j)}{1 + 4} = \\frac{-2j -4j^2}{5} = \\frac{4 - 2j}{5} = \\frac{4}{5} - j\\frac{2}{5} $\n\nSince $ \\cos t $ has components at $ \\omega = \\pm1 $, the output is the inverse transform:  \n$ y(t) = \\text{Re}\\left[ H(j1) \\cdot e^{j t} \\right] = \\text{Re}\\left[ \\left(\\frac{4}{5} + j\\frac{2}{5}\\right)(\\cos t + j \\sin t) \\right] $\n\nCompute:  \n$ = \\frac{4}{5}\\cos t - \\frac{2}{5}\\sin t $ (imaginary parts cancel in real response)\n\nThus, $ y(t) = \\frac{4}{5}\\cos t - \\frac{2}{5}\\sin t $\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 294,
        "output_tokens": 534,
        "total_tokens": 828
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
