      "generated_answer": "The best available evidence for the association between sugar intake and dental caries, given that randomized controlled trials are unethical for long-term harmful exposure, comes from observational studies that track exposure and outcome over time. A **Cohort study** is the specific epidemiological design that follows groups (cohorts) with different sugar intakes to compare the incidence of dental caries, establishing temporality and minimizing recall bias compared to case-control studies. While longitudinal in nature, \"Cohort\" is the precise scientific term for this design, making it the superior choice over the broader descriptor \"Longitudinal\".\n\n\\boxed{I}",
