    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe study found that older persons with high financial assets accepted preventive home visits more frequently than those with low assets (adjusted OR = 1.5, 95% CI: 1.1-2.0), which indicates a statistically significant association between socioeconomic status and acceptance rates, demonstrating a social imbalance.",
