      "generated_answer": "The histologic evaluation found viable germ cell elements in 14% of testicular remnants, and an additional 7% had seminiferous tubules, suggesting some potential for functional tissue. This indicates that surgical exploration and removal may be warranted in certain cases to evaluate or preserve fertility potential. Therefore, the findings support a recommendation for surgical management.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
      "success": true,
