      "generated_answer": "The poem discusses the inability of families to pay the \"land tax\" because the men have been conscripted and are not returning (\"Shanxi troops were never sent home\"). This situation provides direct evidence for the Tang Dynasty's heavy reliance on conscription to meet military needs, as the men are taken away indefinitely, leaving the agricultural labor force depleted and unable to meet tax obligations.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
