      "generated_answer": "The Populist Party Platform of 1892 criticizes corporate monopolies, national banks, trusts, and the exploitation of farmers and working people by powerful financial interests. The platform explicitly calls for returning government to \"the plain people\" in response to perceived corruption and economic injustice. This aligns most directly with growing rural opposition to corporate and banking power.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
