    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4841",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"If any person or persons shall, from and after the passing of this act, by force and violence, take and carry away, or cause to be taken or carried away, and shall, by fraud or false pretense, seduce, or cause to be seduced, or shall attempt so to take, carry away or seduce, any negro or mulatto, from any part or parts of this commonwealth, to any other place or places whatsoever, out of this commonwealth, with a design and intention of selling and disposing of, or of causing to be sold, or of keeping and detaining, or of causing to be kept and detained, such negro or mulatto, as a slave or servant for life, or for any term whatsoever, every such person or persons, his or their aiders or abettors, shall on conviction thereof, in any court of this commonwealth having competent jurisdiction, be deemed guilty of a felony.\"\n—Excerpt from Pennsylvania law, 1826\nThe passage and implementation of this Pennsylvania law reflected an ongoing conflict between\n\nOptions: \nA. supporters and opponents of government regulation of commerce.\nB. rural and urban interests.\nC. the legal system and the public's moral sentiment.\nD. those who favored the abolition of slavery and those who wanted to maintain the status quo.\nE. federal law and state law.\nF. economic interests and humanitarian concerns.\nG. Northern and Southern states over the issue of slavery.\nH. the principles of capitalism and socialism.\nI. those who favored gradual emancipation and those who favored immediate emancipation.\nJ. the rights of individuals and the power of the state.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "z-ai/glm-4.7",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Pennsylvania law of 1826 was designed to protect free Black residents from being kidnapped and taken to slave states to be sold into slavery. This directly reflects the growing sectional conflict between Northern states (which were gradually abolishing slavery) and Southern states (which were maintaining and expanding slavery). The law demonstrates how Pennsylvania was asserting its position as a free state against attempts by slaveholders to extend the institution of slavery.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
